# Code owners for Withe — https://docs.github.com/articles/about-code-owners
#
# GitHub auto-requests review from the owner on matching PRs. Branch protection
# does not require code-owner review (a solo project has no second approver), but
# declaring ownership is good hygiene and makes required review a one-line switch
# if the maintainer set grows.

* @schubydoo

# Renovate-managed and generated paths — no owner, so dependency and regeneration
# PRs don't auto-request a review that would only rubber-stamp them.
/package-lock.json
/Dockerfile
/.github/workflows/
/spec/openapi-community.yaml
/src/adapters/ce/generated/
